1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,500
Twelve years before the end of the world,

2
00:00:02,350 --> 00:00:05,020
a young girl woke screaming from a dream.

3
00:00:05,810 --> 00:00:07,520
She had seen her city burn.

4
00:00:08,470 --> 00:00:09,540
Mountains split open.

5
00:00:09,770 --> 00:00:14,810
The sky turned black, and a sea of fire
swallowed the greatest empire men

6
00:00:14,660 --> 00:00:15,710
had ever built.

7
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:17,710
Her father believed her.

8
00:00:18,110 --> 00:00:22,380
He sold everything he owned, gathered
his family and five dragons,

9
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:25,500
and sailed to a lonely rock
at the edge of the world.

10
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:28,700
Twelve years later, the dream came true.

11
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:33,060
That girl's family would conquer a continent
with three dragons and fewer

12
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:34,380
than sixteen hundred men.

13
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:39,200
They would sit on a throne of melted swords
for almost three hundred years.

14
00:00:39,710 --> 00:00:42,260
They would build, and they would burn.

15
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:47,700
And in the end, they would tear each
other apart in a war that killed the

16
00:00:47,550 --> 00:00:48,620
dragons themselves.

17
00:00:49,530 --> 00:00:52,180
And the last of them is still out there.

18
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:57,020
In the books, she is a young
queen, far across the sea,

19
00:00:57,210 --> 00:00:59,080
with three dragons of her own.

20
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:02,450
This is the complete history
of House Targaryen.

21
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:11,570
Before we begin, a word about
where this story comes from.

22
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:16,610
In the books, the history of House Targaryen
is written by a maester of

23
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:19,190
the Citadel, Archmaester Gyldayn.

24
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:21,850
He did not see any of it.

25
00:01:22,200 --> 00:01:24,640
He stitched it together
from older accounts.

26
00:01:25,270 --> 00:01:28,980
One came from a pious septon
who flattered the kings.

27
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:32,840
One came from a grand maester
who tried to be fair.

28
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:36,880
And one came from a court
fool named Mushroom,

29
00:01:37,330 --> 00:01:41,240
who claimed he had been hiding in
every bedchamber in the Red Keep.

30
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:43,520
They often disagree.

31
00:01:43,720 --> 00:01:46,570
So when this video says
"the histories say",

32
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:51,390
remember: even inside the story, nobody
is completely sure what happened.

33
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,430
Now, the dream.

34
00:01:54,080 --> 00:01:56,850
More than four hundred years
before the main books,

35
00:01:57,180 --> 00:02:00,250
the Freehold of Valyria ruled
half the known world.

36
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:01,830
It was not a kingdom.

37
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:06,110
It was a freehold, ruled by some forty
great families of dragonlords,

38
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:11,110
who flew over their empire on dragons
and mined its fire mountains for gold

39
00:02:10,960 --> 00:02:12,590
and slaves and power.

40
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:15,470
The Targaryens were one of those families.

41
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:17,000
They were not the richest.

42
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:18,550
They were not the strongest.

43
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:20,130
They were not even close.

44
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:24,410
Then Lord Aenar Targaryen's
maiden daughter had a dream.

45
00:02:24,810 --> 00:02:27,340
The histories call her Daenys the Dreamer.

46
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:29,420
She saw Valyria destroyed.

47
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:30,840
Aenar believed her.

48
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:34,770
He sold his lands in the Freehold,
and moved his whole house,

49
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:37,110
with all its wealth and its five dragons,

50
00:02:37,480 --> 00:02:41,910
to Dragonstone, a smoking island
at the mouth of Blackwater Bay.

51
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,580
It was the westernmost outpost of Valyria,

52
00:02:45,730 --> 00:02:48,160
a lonely rock on the edge of nowhere.

53
00:02:48,950 --> 00:02:50,920
The other dragonlords mocked him.

54
00:02:51,430 --> 00:02:54,640
A great lord, running from
a girl's nightmare.

55
00:02:55,610 --> 00:02:58,900
Twelve years later, the
Fourteen Flames woke.

56
00:02:59,650 --> 00:03:05,200
The histories say every hill for five
hundred miles split open on the same

57
00:03:05,050 --> 00:03:05,620
day.

58
00:03:06,290 --> 00:03:12,820
Fire and ash filled the sky, so thick
and so hot that even dragons fell

59
00:03:12,670 --> 00:03:14,080
burning from the air.

60
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:15,900
Lakes boiled.

61
00:03:16,770 --> 00:03:18,920
Palaces and temples crumbled.

62
00:03:19,490 --> 00:03:22,300
The sea rushed in and swallowed
what was left.

63
00:03:23,050 --> 00:03:25,360
Nobody agrees on what caused it.

64
00:03:25,870 --> 00:03:28,440
Some say the fire mountains
simply erupted.

65
00:03:29,030 --> 00:03:31,600
Some say the Valyrians dug too deep.

66
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:36,310
Some say the spells that held the mountains
quiet for five thousand years

67
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,370
finally failed.

68
00:03:37,840 --> 00:03:40,210
The maesters just call it the Doom.

69
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:43,630
When it was over, the Freehold was gone.

70
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:46,560
Its dragonlords, its cities, its sorcery,

71
00:03:46,690 --> 00:03:48,600
nearly every dragon in the world.

72
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,450
Where Valyria had stood, there was only
a broken scatter of islands in a

73
00:03:53,300 --> 00:03:57,130
dark, steaming water that sailors
still call the Smoking Sea.

74
00:03:57,720 --> 00:04:02,270
Even now, in the books, men say no
ship that sails there returns.

75
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:06,950
Only one dragonlord family survived
with its dragons intact.

76
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:10,150
The family that had listened
to a girl's dream.

77
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:14,110
What followed is called
the Century of Blood.

78
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:18,990
The free cities of the east tore each
other apart over Valyria's corpse.

79
00:04:19,390 --> 00:04:24,750
And for a hundred years, the Targaryens
mostly stayed out of it.

80
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:31,030
They sat on Dragonstone, looking
east, toward the ruins of home.

81
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:33,760
Then a boy named Aegon was born.

82
00:04:34,470 --> 00:04:36,080
And Aegon looked west.

83
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:42,210
Aegon Targaryen grew up in a castle
that looked like a nightmare.

84
00:04:42,900 --> 00:04:45,730
The Valyrians had raised
Dragonstone with magic,

85
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:48,590
shaping the black stone like soft clay.

86
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:53,950
Its towers were carved as dragons, hunched
along the walls as if about to

87
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,510
take flight.

88
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:58,590
Its gates were open dragon mouths.

89
00:04:58,990 --> 00:05:02,420
Gargoyles and stone wyverns
crouched everywhere,

90
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:06,320
and the whole mountain beneath
it steamed and rumbled.

91
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:11,260
He had two sisters, and
in the old Valyrian way,

92
00:05:11,610 --> 00:05:15,800
to keep the blood of the dragon
pure, he married them both.

93
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:19,300
The histories say he married
Visenya first,

94
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:23,000
out of duty, and Rhaenys out of love.

95
00:05:23,670 --> 00:05:25,900
They could not have been more different.

96
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:28,410
Visenya, the elder, was a warrior.

97
00:05:29,060 --> 00:05:31,010
Stern, severe, hard to impress.

98
00:05:31,400 --> 00:05:33,440
She trained with the sword from girlhood,

99
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:36,800
and she carried a blade of Valyrian
steel called Dark Sister.

100
00:05:37,830 --> 00:05:41,100
Rhaenys, the younger, was bright
and playful and curious.

101
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:44,410
She loved music, and dancing,
and clever company.

102
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:46,730
She filled her halls with singers.

103
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:50,360
And she flew her dragon simply
because she loved to fly.

104
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:53,440
Aegon himself was the hardest to read.

105
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:57,530
The histories describe
him as grave and quiet,

106
00:05:57,840 --> 00:05:59,810
a man who kept his own counsel.

107
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:04,390
He carried his own Valyrian sword,
a black blade called Blackfyre.

108
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:06,940
And each of them had a dragon.

109
00:06:07,670 --> 00:06:09,060
Visenya rode Vhagar.

110
00:06:09,730 --> 00:06:11,000
Rhaenys rode Meraxes.

111
00:06:11,470 --> 00:06:13,860
And Aegon rode the greatest of them all.

112
00:06:14,930 --> 00:06:16,740
Balerion, the Black Dread.

113
00:06:17,450 --> 00:06:21,540
Balerion was the last living dragon
to have seen Valyria itself.

114
00:06:22,070 --> 00:06:23,520
His scales were black.

115
00:06:23,370 --> 00:06:26,250
His fire was black.

116
00:06:26,650 --> 00:06:31,920
When he flew, the stories say, his shadow
fell over whole towns at once,

117
00:06:32,210 --> 00:06:36,340
and people in the streets below would
look up and see the sun go out.

118
00:06:37,170 --> 00:06:41,860
In the first book, a young Arya Stark
gets lost in the cellars of the Red

119
00:06:41,710 --> 00:06:44,880
Keep and finds the old dragon
skulls in the dark.

120
00:06:45,690 --> 00:06:48,580
The biggest of them has
teeth like black swords,

121
00:06:48,430 --> 00:06:52,720
and a jaw so wide it could swallow
a horse and rider whole.

122
00:06:53,270 --> 00:06:55,140
That was Balerion.

123
00:06:57,010 --> 00:07:01,400
In the great hall of Dragonstone,
Aegon had a table made.

124
00:07:01,970 --> 00:07:06,780
Fifty feet long, cut in the shape of Westeros
and painted with every forest,

125
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:09,240
river, city and castle on the continent.

126
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:12,640
And on it, there were no borders.

127
00:07:13,410 --> 00:07:14,480
No kingdoms.

128
00:07:14,950 --> 00:07:16,680
Just one land.

129
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:21,570
Centuries later, in the books, Stannis
Baratheon would stand at the same

130
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,970
table and brood over the same map.

131
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:27,790
Because when Aegon looked
across the narrow sea,

132
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:29,930
he did not see one land.

133
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:33,730
He saw seven kingdoms,
each with its own king,

134
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,430
and all of them at war.

135
00:07:35,830 --> 00:07:38,140
In the North, the Starks of Winterfell.

136
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,910
In the Vale, the Arryns of the Eyrie.

137
00:07:41,310 --> 00:07:44,180
In the west, the Lannisters
of Casterly Rock.

138
00:07:44,030 --> 00:07:47,550
In the Reach, the Gardeners of Highgarden.

139
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:51,240
In the Stormlands, the Durrandons
of Storm's End.

140
00:07:51,650 --> 00:07:53,960
In the south, the Martells of Dorne.

141
00:07:54,490 --> 00:07:59,800
And in the riverlands, a cruel king from
the Iron Islands named Harren the

142
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:04,440
Black, who had just finished building
the largest castle the world had ever

143
00:08:04,290 --> 00:08:04,920
seen.

144
00:08:05,890 --> 00:08:07,720
Why did Aegon go west?

145
00:08:08,470 --> 00:08:10,200
The histories do not agree.

146
00:08:10,610 --> 00:08:12,930
Some say it was simple ambition.

147
00:08:12,780 --> 00:08:16,910
Some say Daenys's old dream had
shown more than the Doom.

148
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,730
Others point to an insult.

149
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:24,390
The storm king, Argilac the Arrogant,
offered Aegon a marriage alliance.

150
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:25,950
Aegon countered.

151
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:31,250
And Argilac sent back an answer so insulting
that there could only be one

152
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:31,770
reply.

153
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:35,810
In the show House of the Dragon,
there is another reason.

154
00:08:36,560 --> 00:08:40,490
Aegon has a secret dream of a great
winter coming from the north,

155
00:08:40,340 --> 00:08:44,150
and conquers Westeros to unite
it against the dead.

156
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:47,930
That prophecy is passed from king to heir,

157
00:08:47,780 --> 00:08:49,770
all the way down to Daenerys.

158
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:52,150
It is a powerful idea.

159
00:08:52,660 --> 00:08:54,690
But it is the show's invention.

160
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:58,370
In the books, no such dream
is ever mentioned.

161
00:09:01,025 --> 00:09:03,735
Aegon landed at the mouth
of the Blackwater Rush,

162
00:09:04,005 --> 00:09:06,955
on three hills above a fishing village.

163
00:09:06,805 --> 00:09:10,805
He brought fewer than sixteen hundred men.

164
00:09:11,005 --> 00:09:14,535
On the highest hill, he built a
rough fort of timber and earth.

165
00:09:14,935 --> 00:09:15,985
The Aegonfort.

166
00:09:16,775 --> 00:09:21,105
One day it would become the Red Keep,
and the village below would grow into

167
00:09:20,955 --> 00:09:22,625
a city called King's Landing.

168
00:09:23,455 --> 00:09:26,185
Westeros still counts its
years from his conquest.

169
00:09:27,075 --> 00:09:31,065
In the books, every date is so
many years After the Conquest.

170
00:09:31,695 --> 00:09:32,225
A.C.

171
00:09:32,745 --> 00:09:35,325
The first great test came
in the riverlands.

172
00:09:35,915 --> 00:09:38,965
Harren the Black had spent forty
years building Harrenhal.

173
00:09:38,815 --> 00:09:43,995
Its walls were so high that no
siege tower could reach them.

174
00:09:44,325 --> 00:09:47,065
Its five towers were the
tallest in the realm.

175
00:09:47,495 --> 00:09:49,505
Its great hall could feast an army.

176
00:09:50,155 --> 00:09:54,185
And the histories say it was finished
on the very day Aegon landed.

177
00:09:54,955 --> 00:09:57,125
Harren believed stone could not burn.

178
00:09:57,635 --> 00:10:00,705
He shut himself inside with
his sons, and he waited.

179
00:10:01,575 --> 00:10:03,385
Aegon did not besiege the castle.

180
00:10:03,785 --> 00:10:06,415
He flew over the walls
at dusk on Balerion.

181
00:10:06,815 --> 00:10:09,565
And the black fire poured
down into the towers.

182
00:10:10,095 --> 00:10:12,965
Stone, it turns out, does
not need to burn.

183
00:10:13,365 --> 00:10:15,315
It only needs to get hot enough.

184
00:10:15,845 --> 00:10:17,915
The towers became ovens.

185
00:10:18,105 --> 00:10:23,145
The great stones cracked, and glowed,
and ran like candle wax.

186
00:10:24,275 --> 00:10:27,845
By morning, Harren the Black
and his sons were gone,

187
00:10:28,055 --> 00:10:29,725
and his line with them.

188
00:10:30,435 --> 00:10:32,785
Three hundred years later, in the books,

189
00:10:33,175 --> 00:10:37,905
Harrenhal still stands half-ruined,
its towers twisted and melted.

190
00:10:38,085 --> 00:10:39,985
People say it is cursed.

191
00:10:40,715 --> 00:10:45,285
Nearly every lord who has held
it since has come to a bad end.

192
00:10:46,755 --> 00:10:50,045
In the south, Aegon's half-brother
and general,

193
00:10:50,395 --> 00:10:54,665
Orys Baratheon, faced the storm
king, Argilac the Arrogant,

194
00:10:54,915 --> 00:10:57,525
who had insulted Aegon in the first place.

195
00:10:58,235 --> 00:10:59,965
Argilac fell in the battle.

196
00:11:00,164 --> 00:11:03,494
Orys married the dead king's daughter,
and took his castle,

197
00:11:03,605 --> 00:11:05,914
his banners and his words for his own.

198
00:11:06,344 --> 00:11:08,594
That is how House Baratheon began.

199
00:11:08,995 --> 00:11:11,164
As a Targaryen general's reward.

200
00:11:11,774 --> 00:11:13,924
Then came the moment that
decided everything.

201
00:11:14,294 --> 00:11:18,794
Two kings joined forces against the dragons:
Loren Lannister of the Rock,

202
00:11:18,644 --> 00:11:20,734
and Mern Gardener of the Reach.

203
00:11:21,184 --> 00:11:23,874
Together they marched with
fifty-five thousand men,

204
00:11:24,184 --> 00:11:26,734
the largest army Westeros had ever seen.

205
00:11:27,365 --> 00:11:29,174
Aegon had about eleven thousand.

206
00:11:29,574 --> 00:11:32,625
They met on open ground
south of the Blackwater,

207
00:11:32,755 --> 00:11:35,724
in a dry summer, with the
grass high and golden.

208
00:11:36,174 --> 00:11:38,444
For the first and only time in history,

209
00:11:38,594 --> 00:11:41,025
all three dragons flew
into battle together.

210
00:11:41,424 --> 00:11:42,015
Vhagar.

211
00:11:42,414 --> 00:11:43,084
Meraxes.

212
00:11:43,485 --> 00:11:44,294
And Balerion.

213
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:46,454
The grass caught at once.

214
00:11:46,855 --> 00:11:48,525
The wind did the rest.

215
00:11:49,014 --> 00:11:52,184
The histories say four thousand
men burned that day.

216
00:11:52,875 --> 00:11:54,984
Mern Gardener, the last king of the Reach,

217
00:11:55,214 --> 00:11:59,844
died with his sons and his grandsons,
and his line ended on that field.

218
00:12:00,475 --> 00:12:01,625
Loren Lannister lived.

219
00:12:02,024 --> 00:12:05,074
He knelt, and laid his
crown at Aegon's feet.

220
00:12:05,764 --> 00:12:07,734
The battle has a name in the books.

221
00:12:08,135 --> 00:12:09,865
They call it the Field of Fire.

222
00:12:10,715 --> 00:12:13,724
After that, the kingdoms
fell like dominoes.

223
00:12:14,054 --> 00:12:18,554
In the Vale, the Arryns' queen regent
believed the Eyrie could never fall.

224
00:12:18,924 --> 00:12:21,744
It stood on a mountain,
high above any army.

225
00:12:22,294 --> 00:12:25,084
But no castle is high enough
to stop a dragon.

226
00:12:25,755 --> 00:12:31,164
Visenya simply flew Vhagar up the mountain
and landed in the castle yard.

227
00:12:32,014 --> 00:12:34,405
The boy king of the Vale, Ronnel Arryn,

228
00:12:34,495 --> 00:12:38,645
was taken up on Vhagar's back, flown
three times around the mountain,

229
00:12:38,875 --> 00:12:41,365
and came down to surrender his crown.

230
00:12:41,564 --> 00:12:45,454
In the North, Torrhen Stark marched
south with thirty thousand men.

231
00:12:45,984 --> 00:12:48,494
When he reached the Trident
and saw the dragons,

232
00:12:48,344 --> 00:12:50,914
and heard what had happened to Harrenhal,

233
00:12:51,124 --> 00:12:54,054
he made the hardest choice
a king can make.

234
00:12:54,454 --> 00:12:55,404
He knelt.

235
00:12:56,074 --> 00:12:59,044
The North remembers him
as the King Who Knelt.

236
00:12:59,454 --> 00:13:02,624
But because he knelt, Winterfell
never burned.

237
00:13:03,134 --> 00:13:07,324
And in Oldtown, the High Septon
of the Faith prayed for a sign.

238
00:13:07,724 --> 00:13:11,094
The gods, he said, told
him not to oppose Aegon.

239
00:13:11,504 --> 00:13:16,234
So the city opened its gates, and the
High Septon anointed Aegon king with

240
00:13:16,084 --> 00:13:17,114
the seven oils.

241
00:13:18,104 --> 00:13:19,654
Aegon now needed a throne.

242
00:13:20,054 --> 00:13:23,444
He had the swords of his fallen
enemies gathered together,

243
00:13:23,654 --> 00:13:28,304
the songs say a thousand of them, and
had them heated in Balerion's fire,

244
00:13:28,534 --> 00:13:31,044
then beaten and twisted into a seat.

245
00:13:31,694 --> 00:13:35,324
In the show, the Iron Throne is a neat,

246
00:13:35,574 --> 00:13:36,644
upright chair.

247
00:13:37,044 --> 00:13:40,014
In the books, it is something
else entirely.

248
00:13:40,414 --> 00:13:45,464
An asymmetric monstrosity of spikes,
jagged edges and twisted metal,

249
00:13:45,894 --> 00:13:49,564
rising high above the hall,
reached by steep iron steps.

250
00:13:50,134 --> 00:13:51,884
It was meant to be uncomfortable.

251
00:13:52,574 --> 00:13:56,264
The histories say Aegon
wanted it that way.

252
00:13:56,664 --> 00:13:59,414
A king, he said, should never sit easy.

253
00:14:00,044 --> 00:14:01,614
And the throne was dangerous.

254
00:14:02,424 --> 00:14:04,934
Kings who sat on it cut themselves
on its blades.

255
00:14:06,224 --> 00:14:10,714
Later, people would whisper that the
throne itself judged who was worthy,

256
00:14:10,564 --> 00:14:13,374
and drew the blood of those who were not.

257
00:14:14,664 --> 00:14:16,374
Six kingdoms had fallen.

258
00:14:16,964 --> 00:14:18,194
One had not.

259
00:14:19,164 --> 00:14:24,134
Dorne was a hot, dry land of deserts,
red mountains and scorpions.

260
00:14:24,964 --> 00:14:27,134
And the Dornish had learned
from the Field of Fire.

261
00:14:27,984 --> 00:14:29,494
They refused to give battle.

262
00:14:29,694 --> 00:14:33,124
When the dragons came, their armies
simply melted into the desert.

263
00:14:33,524 --> 00:14:35,594
When the dragons left, they came back.

264
00:14:36,244 --> 00:14:38,694
Then, in the tenth year after the landing,

265
00:14:39,184 --> 00:14:42,354
Rhaenys and Meraxes flew over
the castle of Hellholt.

266
00:14:42,664 --> 00:14:46,844
A bolt from a great Dornish scorpion
struck Meraxes through the eye.

267
00:14:47,194 --> 00:14:48,474
The dragon fell.

268
00:14:49,044 --> 00:14:50,534
And Rhaenys fell with her.

269
00:14:51,264 --> 00:14:53,854
Aegon's answer is remembered
as the Dragon's Wroth.

270
00:14:54,304 --> 00:14:59,374
For two years, Aegon and Visenya burned
every Dornish castle they could

271
00:14:59,224 --> 00:14:59,834
reach.

272
00:15:00,624 --> 00:15:02,194
Dorne still would not bend.

273
00:15:03,504 --> 00:15:06,454
In the end, a letter arrived
from the Princess of Dorne.

274
00:15:07,144 --> 00:15:08,194
Aegon read it alone.

275
00:15:08,644 --> 00:15:10,014
No one knows what it said.

276
00:15:10,424 --> 00:15:15,054
But after he read it, he made peace,
and never went to war in Dorne again.

277
00:15:16,024 --> 00:15:17,914
Aegon ruled for thirty-seven years.

278
00:15:17,764 --> 00:15:22,564
He died in his bed on
Dragonstone, in peace,

279
00:15:22,934 --> 00:15:24,164
at the head of a dynasty.

280
00:15:24,874 --> 00:15:27,384
His family would not stay
at peace for long.

281
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,750
If you are enjoying this journey
through the history of Westeros,

282
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,770
subscribe to the Mythic Archives.

283
00:15:34,170 --> 00:15:36,820
We bring the books to life: the stories,

284
00:15:37,150 --> 00:15:41,100
the history, and the small details
that make these worlds feel real.

285
00:15:42,490 --> 00:15:44,500
Now, the sons of the dragon.

286
00:15:47,820 --> 00:15:51,570
Aegon left two sons, by
two different sisters.

287
00:15:52,240 --> 00:15:56,690
Each was raised by his own mother,
and each became a mirror of her.

288
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:01,410
Aenys, the son of Rhaenys,
was gentle and dreamy,

289
00:16:01,640 --> 00:16:05,550
often sick as a boy, kind
and eager to be loved.

290
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:09,490
Maegor, the son of Visenya,
was the opposite.

291
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:14,110
Huge, strong, and fearless,
a warrior from childhood,

292
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:17,730
with his mother's iron and none
of his father's patience.

293
00:16:18,960 --> 00:16:20,090
Aenys got the throne.

294
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:23,490
Maegor got his father's sword, Blackfyre.

295
00:16:23,688 --> 00:16:25,878
Aenys wanted everyone to love him.

296
00:16:26,308 --> 00:16:28,818
Instead, the realm rose against him.

297
00:16:29,228 --> 00:16:30,858
The biggest threat was the Faith.

298
00:16:31,268 --> 00:16:34,258
Its holy orders, the Warrior's
Sons and the Poor Fellows,

299
00:16:34,268 --> 00:16:37,598
had always hated the Targaryen custom
of marrying brother to sister.

300
00:16:38,248 --> 00:16:40,858
When Aenys married his own
daughter to his son,

301
00:16:41,188 --> 00:16:43,398
the High Septon called him an abomination.

302
00:16:43,798 --> 00:16:46,208
The Faith Militant rose across the realm.

303
00:16:46,718 --> 00:16:47,868
Aenys never recovered.

304
00:16:48,358 --> 00:16:51,008
He died after just five
years on the throne.

305
00:16:51,738 --> 00:16:54,828
Some whispered that Visenya
had helped him on his way,

306
00:16:54,958 --> 00:16:56,028
with one of her potions.

307
00:16:56,858 --> 00:16:58,088
Then came Maegor.

308
00:16:58,798 --> 00:17:03,028
He seized the throne, and claimed the
greatest prize of all: Balerion,

309
00:17:03,238 --> 00:17:05,708
the Black Dread, who had
flown under his father,

310
00:17:05,558 --> 00:17:07,208
and now flew under him.

311
00:17:07,858 --> 00:17:10,268
Maegor met the Faith with fire and steel.

312
00:17:10,668 --> 00:17:12,258
He crushed the Warrior's Sons.

313
00:17:13,028 --> 00:17:16,578
When his own nephew rose against him,
he met him over the Gods Eye,

314
00:17:16,428 --> 00:17:20,418
dragon against dragon, and the
nephew did not come back.

315
00:17:20,818 --> 00:17:24,568
He finished the Red Keep, and the histories
say that when it was done,

316
00:17:24,678 --> 00:17:29,348
he had the builders put to death, so that
no one would ever know its secret

317
00:17:29,198 --> 00:17:29,848
passages.

318
00:17:30,378 --> 00:17:32,448
He married six times.

319
00:17:33,138 --> 00:17:36,248
Three of those wives he
wed on a single day.

320
00:17:36,698 --> 00:17:38,968
The court called them the Black Brides.

321
00:17:39,368 --> 00:17:43,098
And for all those marriages,
Maegor had no living heir.

322
00:17:43,498 --> 00:17:47,628
The histories record only stillbirths,
and dark rumours of curses.

323
00:17:48,378 --> 00:17:51,708
Within six years, the realm
turned against him.

324
00:17:52,178 --> 00:17:56,688
His lords left him one by one, to
join his young nephew Jaehaerys,

325
00:17:56,858 --> 00:18:00,308
who had come out of hiding
with a dragon of his own.

326
00:18:00,508 --> 00:18:03,118
One morning, Maegor the
Cruel was found dead,

327
00:18:03,408 --> 00:18:04,798
sitting upon the Iron Throne.

328
00:18:05,388 --> 00:18:06,618
Nobody knows what happened.

329
00:18:07,018 --> 00:18:08,428
Some say he took his own life.

330
00:18:08,828 --> 00:18:10,238
Some say someone helped him.

331
00:18:10,638 --> 00:18:13,808
And some say the throne itself
finally made its judgement.

332
00:18:16,509 --> 00:18:20,159
The boy who took the throne after
Maegor was fourteen years old.

333
00:18:20,559 --> 00:18:21,869
His name was Jaehaerys.

334
00:18:22,269 --> 00:18:24,159
He would rule for fifty-five years.

335
00:18:24,489 --> 00:18:29,389
And to this day, in the books, he is remembered
as the wisest king who ever

336
00:18:29,239 --> 00:18:30,529
sat on the Iron Throne.

337
00:18:31,019 --> 00:18:32,209
He was not alone.

338
00:18:32,609 --> 00:18:36,559
He married his sister Alysanne,
clever and warm and fearless,

339
00:18:36,769 --> 00:18:38,979
and the histories call her the Good Queen.

340
00:18:39,769 --> 00:18:42,359
Together, on the dragons
Vermithor and Silverwing,

341
00:18:42,569 --> 00:18:44,419
they flew to every corner of the realm.

342
00:18:44,849 --> 00:18:47,639
And they did something
no Targaryen had tried.

343
00:18:48,039 --> 00:18:49,429
They made the realm work.

344
00:18:49,999 --> 00:18:52,049
First, they made peace with the Faith.

345
00:18:53,039 --> 00:18:55,989
Jaehaerys's Hand, a wise
septon named Barth,

346
00:18:56,259 --> 00:18:59,109
struck a bargain: the crown
would protect the Faith,

347
00:18:59,159 --> 00:19:02,209
and in return, the Faith would
lay down its swords forever.

348
00:19:02,459 --> 00:19:04,579
The Faith Militant was disbanded.

349
00:19:05,029 --> 00:19:08,379
And the Targaryens' marriages
were declared an exception,

350
00:19:08,749 --> 00:19:12,799
blessed by the gods, because the dragonlords
were not like other men.

351
00:19:14,089 --> 00:19:15,159
Then they built.

352
00:19:15,989 --> 00:19:19,039
Jaehaerys gave the realm one
law, instead of seven.

353
00:19:19,689 --> 00:19:23,379
He built roads across Westeros,
including the Kingsroad,

354
00:19:23,529 --> 00:19:26,699
which runs from King's Landing
all the way to the Wall.

355
00:19:27,489 --> 00:19:30,499
He gave King's Landing wells and sewers.

356
00:19:30,899 --> 00:19:32,469
He gave the realm peace.

357
00:19:33,079 --> 00:19:35,469
And Alysanne changed the lives of women.

358
00:19:35,668 --> 00:19:39,698
She persuaded the king to abolish the
lord's right to the first night,

359
00:19:40,048 --> 00:19:43,858
an old custom that let a lord claim
any bride on her wedding night.

360
00:19:44,368 --> 00:19:48,538
She flew Silverwing to the Wall, and
gave the Night's Watch new lands to

361
00:19:48,388 --> 00:19:49,298
feed the brothers.

362
00:19:49,708 --> 00:19:52,198
To this day, the land is
called the New Gift.

363
00:19:52,708 --> 00:19:57,538
And at Castle Black, the gate the Watch
renamed in her honour is still called

364
00:19:57,388 --> 00:19:58,478
the Queensgate.

365
00:19:59,068 --> 00:20:01,478
But the long reign had a sad heart.

366
00:20:02,168 --> 00:20:04,998
Jaehaerys and Alysanne
had thirteen children,

367
00:20:04,848 --> 00:20:06,878
and outlived most of them.

368
00:20:07,148 --> 00:20:11,308
Their heir, Prince Aemon, was killed
by raiders on the island of Tarth.

369
00:20:11,778 --> 00:20:15,448
Years later, their second
son, Baelon, died too.

370
00:20:16,038 --> 00:20:18,928
And that raised a question that
would haunt the family.

371
00:20:19,378 --> 00:20:20,768
Who inherits next?

372
00:20:21,238 --> 00:20:23,568
Aemon had left a daughter, Rhaenys.

373
00:20:23,968 --> 00:20:26,198
Baelon had left a son, Viserys.

374
00:20:26,598 --> 00:20:29,208
In the hundred and first
year after the Conquest,

375
00:20:29,418 --> 00:20:32,068
Jaehaerys called a Great
Council at Harrenhal,

376
00:20:31,918 --> 00:20:34,828
and let the lords of the realm decide.

377
00:20:35,228 --> 00:20:36,878
The lords chose Viserys.

378
00:20:37,278 --> 00:20:38,968
A man, over a woman.

379
00:20:39,538 --> 00:20:42,588
The histories call Rhaenys
the Queen Who Never Was.

380
00:20:43,018 --> 00:20:44,708
It seemed to settle things.

381
00:20:45,138 --> 00:20:49,348
In fact, it set a precedent that
would rip the dynasty in half.

382
00:20:50,238 --> 00:20:53,348
When the Old King died, the
whole realm mourned him.

383
00:20:53,748 --> 00:20:56,078
His dragons had lived to be ancient.

384
00:20:56,478 --> 00:20:58,768
His peace had lasted half a century.

385
00:20:59,358 --> 00:21:01,508
It would not survive his grandson.

386
00:21:04,112 --> 00:21:07,122
King Viserys the First was kind, generous,

387
00:21:07,372 --> 00:21:09,702
and fond of feasts and tourneys.

388
00:21:10,312 --> 00:21:12,822
He wanted, above all, to be liked.

389
00:21:13,332 --> 00:21:16,282
He also ruled at the very
height of Targaryen power.

390
00:21:16,682 --> 00:21:19,592
There were more dragons in
the realm than ever before.

391
00:21:19,792 --> 00:21:23,642
In the books, the histories call this
the high summer of House Targaryen.

392
00:21:24,132 --> 00:21:27,702
Viserys had one living child by
his first wife: a daughter,

393
00:21:27,932 --> 00:21:28,382
Rhaenyra.

394
00:21:28,732 --> 00:21:31,132
The court called her the Realm's Delight.

395
00:21:31,822 --> 00:21:35,692
When his wife died in childbirth, and
the son she bore died with her,

396
00:21:36,122 --> 00:21:38,392
Viserys did something no king had done.

397
00:21:38,822 --> 00:21:40,572
He named his daughter his heir.

398
00:21:40,962 --> 00:21:44,502
And he made the lords of the realm kneel
and swear to defend her right.

399
00:21:44,352 --> 00:21:46,952
Then he married again.

400
00:21:47,352 --> 00:21:51,062
His new queen was Alicent Hightower,
the daughter of his Hand.

401
00:21:51,462 --> 00:21:53,152
And she gave him sons.

402
00:21:53,802 --> 00:21:54,272
Aegon.

403
00:21:54,882 --> 00:21:55,412
Aemond.

404
00:21:56,022 --> 00:21:56,492
Daeron.

405
00:21:57,182 --> 00:21:59,072
Everyone at court could do the arithmetic.

406
00:21:59,782 --> 00:22:04,012
After the Great Council, the realm had
chosen a man over a woman once before.

407
00:22:04,262 --> 00:22:06,302
And now the king had a son.

408
00:22:06,772 --> 00:22:08,942
But Viserys never changed his mind.

409
00:22:09,492 --> 00:22:10,842
Rhaenyra remained his heir.

410
00:22:10,692 --> 00:22:15,972
At a tourney, the histories say,
Queen Alicent wore green,

411
00:22:16,202 --> 00:22:19,912
and Princess Rhaenyra wore the
Targaryen red and black.

412
00:22:20,312 --> 00:22:23,622
From then on, the court
split into two parties.

413
00:22:24,022 --> 00:22:26,532
The greens, who backed Alicent's sons.

414
00:22:26,962 --> 00:22:29,432
And the blacks, who backed Rhaenyra.

415
00:22:30,062 --> 00:22:32,172
Hovering between them was
the king's brother,

416
00:22:32,482 --> 00:22:33,252
Prince Daemon.

417
00:22:33,652 --> 00:22:35,682
Brilliant, reckless, dangerous.

418
00:22:36,252 --> 00:22:39,062
He rode a long red dragon called Caraxes,

419
00:22:39,052 --> 00:22:41,682
the Blood Wyrm, and carried Dark Sister,

420
00:22:41,912 --> 00:22:43,202
Visenya's old sword.

421
00:22:43,712 --> 00:22:47,482
He formed the city watch and
gave them their gold cloaks.

422
00:22:47,972 --> 00:22:50,222
The court called him the Rogue Prince.

423
00:22:50,932 --> 00:22:54,862
In time, Daemon married Rhaenyra,
and joined the blacks.

424
00:22:55,912 --> 00:22:59,682
Rhaenyra's first three sons were
dark-haired and brown-eyed,

425
00:23:00,152 --> 00:23:02,082
nothing like their Velaryon father.

426
00:23:02,672 --> 00:23:05,842
The court whispered about
who their real father was.

427
00:23:06,042 --> 00:23:10,492
And at a funeral on Driftmark, the queen's
young son Aemond climbed onto

428
00:23:10,342 --> 00:23:12,732
the oldest dragon in the world, Vhagar,

429
00:23:12,982 --> 00:23:13,932
and claimed her.

430
00:23:14,622 --> 00:23:16,612
Rhaenyra's boys attacked him for it.

431
00:23:17,082 --> 00:23:19,412
In the fight, Aemond lost an eye.

432
00:23:20,002 --> 00:23:23,752
Later, the histories say, he wore
a sapphire in the empty socket.

433
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:27,402
And he would say he had lost
an eye, but gained a dragon.

434
00:23:28,532 --> 00:23:32,702
In the hundred and twenty-ninth year,
King Viserys died in his sleep.

435
00:23:33,092 --> 00:23:34,812
The greens hid his death.

436
00:23:35,242 --> 00:23:39,572
While the court was kept in the dark, they
crowned Prince Aegon in the Dragonpit

437
00:23:39,422 --> 00:23:40,912
as King Aegon the Second.

438
00:23:41,942 --> 00:23:45,412
On Dragonstone, Rhaenyra
was crowned as queen.

439
00:23:46,042 --> 00:23:47,132
Two monarchs.

440
00:23:47,532 --> 00:23:48,852
Two crowns.

441
00:23:49,002 --> 00:23:50,752
And dragons on both sides.

442
00:23:51,482 --> 00:23:53,812
The first death came in a storm.

443
00:23:54,402 --> 00:23:58,792
Rhaenyra sent her second son, Lucerys,
on his young dragon Arrax,

444
00:23:59,042 --> 00:24:00,892
to win the support of Storm's End.

445
00:24:01,502 --> 00:24:04,172
When he arrived, Aemond was already there,

446
00:24:04,482 --> 00:24:05,232
with Vhagar.

447
00:24:05,632 --> 00:24:09,722
Above Shipbreaker Bay, in a
storm, Vhagar caught Arrax.

448
00:24:10,692 --> 00:24:12,942
Neither the boy nor his dragon survived.

449
00:24:13,712 --> 00:24:17,142
The war that followed is called
the Dance of the Dragons.

450
00:24:17,812 --> 00:24:20,622
It was the darkest chapter
in the family's history.

451
00:24:21,172 --> 00:24:25,482
In revenge for Lucerys, two killers
crept into the Red Keep,

452
00:24:25,332 --> 00:24:27,582
and a child of the greens died.

453
00:24:28,352 --> 00:24:32,042
The histories remember them
only as Blood and Cheese.

454
00:24:33,412 --> 00:24:36,402
At Rook's Rest, the Queen Who Never Was,

455
00:24:36,692 --> 00:24:42,082
Rhaenys, flew her old dragon Meleys against
King Aegon on Sunfyre and Aemond

456
00:24:41,932 --> 00:24:42,682
on Vhagar.

457
00:24:43,592 --> 00:24:44,682
Rhaenys fell.

458
00:24:45,672 --> 00:24:48,682
Aegon survived, horribly burned.

459
00:24:49,632 --> 00:24:51,742
The blacks needed more dragon riders.

460
00:24:52,072 --> 00:24:56,272
So they searched the realm for anyone
with a drop of Targaryen blood.

461
00:24:57,182 --> 00:24:58,772
Bastards, mostly.

462
00:24:58,972 --> 00:25:01,282
Smallfolk who might claim
a dragon and live.

463
00:25:01,892 --> 00:25:04,062
The histories call them the dragonseeds.

464
00:25:04,462 --> 00:25:05,892
Some served with honour.

465
00:25:06,422 --> 00:25:11,332
A thin, dark girl named Nettles tamed a
wild dragon with nothing but patience

466
00:25:11,182 --> 00:25:12,292
and a sheep a day.

467
00:25:12,902 --> 00:25:16,692
But two dragonseeds turned traitor
at the town of Tumbleton,

468
00:25:16,542 --> 00:25:18,212
and handed it to the greens.

469
00:25:19,182 --> 00:25:23,792
In the show, the third season of House
of the Dragon ended at Tumbleton,

470
00:25:23,642 --> 00:25:25,552
in August twenty twenty-six.

471
00:25:26,032 --> 00:25:28,872
The final season is planned
for twenty twenty-eight.

472
00:25:29,402 --> 00:25:33,132
Rhaenyra took King's Landing, and
sat on the Iron Throne herself.

473
00:25:33,662 --> 00:25:36,672
But she was a harsh ruler,
suspicious and grieving,

474
00:25:37,062 --> 00:25:39,232
and the city came to hate her.

475
00:25:40,002 --> 00:25:44,712
One night, a mob led by a prophet called
the Shepherd stormed the Dragonpit.

476
00:25:45,722 --> 00:25:47,892
Dragons are terrifying in the open sky.

477
00:25:48,722 --> 00:25:50,712
Chained in the dark, they
could be overwhelmed.

478
00:25:51,562 --> 00:25:53,112
Several dragons died there.

479
00:25:53,602 --> 00:25:57,792
Rhaenyra's youngest son, Joffrey, died
trying to reach his mother's dragon.

480
00:25:58,192 --> 00:26:00,822
Then came the duel the singers
still sing about.

481
00:26:01,572 --> 00:26:03,342
Prince Daemon waited at Harrenhal.

482
00:26:03,852 --> 00:26:05,722
Aemond came for him on Vhagar.

483
00:26:06,152 --> 00:26:08,862
And above the lake called the Gods Eye,

484
00:26:09,152 --> 00:26:12,062
the two princes met, Caraxes
against Vhagar,

485
00:26:12,392 --> 00:26:15,122
the Blood Wyrm against the
oldest dragon alive.

486
00:26:15,932 --> 00:26:21,442
When Vhagar seized his dragon, Daemon
leapt from Caraxes onto Vhagar's back,

487
00:26:21,292 --> 00:26:23,362
with Dark Sister in his hand.

488
00:26:23,852 --> 00:26:27,902
The histories say he drove it home
through Aemond's empty eye.

489
00:26:28,792 --> 00:26:32,022
Then all of them, two princes
and two dragons,

490
00:26:32,192 --> 00:26:34,082
fell together into the lake.

491
00:26:34,772 --> 00:26:37,942
Rhaenyra fled the city and
sailed to Dragonstone,

492
00:26:38,232 --> 00:26:39,962
hoping to find safety there.

493
00:26:40,162 --> 00:26:42,392
King Aegon the Second was waiting for her,

494
00:26:42,522 --> 00:26:44,292
with his dragon Sunfyre.

495
00:26:44,692 --> 00:26:47,762
He gave his half-sister to the
dragon, and her young son,

496
00:26:47,952 --> 00:26:50,282
also named Aegon, was made to watch.

497
00:26:51,232 --> 00:26:54,102
Aegon the Second did not enjoy
his victory for long.

498
00:26:54,552 --> 00:26:57,642
Within the year, his own
lords poisoned his wine.

499
00:26:58,052 --> 00:26:59,242
The war was over.

500
00:26:59,642 --> 00:27:01,152
And everyone had lost.

501
00:27:02,202 --> 00:27:06,032
In the books, the Dance killed
most of the royal family,

502
00:27:06,402 --> 00:27:08,792
and nearly every dragon in the realm.

503
00:27:09,342 --> 00:27:14,032
A house that had begun the war with
more dragons than ever before ended

504
00:27:13,882 --> 00:27:15,132
it with a handful.

505
00:27:15,542 --> 00:27:19,192
And the boy who had watched
his mother die became king.

506
00:27:21,794 --> 00:27:24,465
The new king was Aegon the Third.

507
00:27:25,075 --> 00:27:29,865
He was only a boy when he was crowned,
and the histories say he was never

508
00:27:29,715 --> 00:27:30,505
young again.

509
00:27:31,115 --> 00:27:33,225
He was melancholy and withdrawn.

510
00:27:33,715 --> 00:27:34,924
He rarely smiled.

511
00:27:35,534 --> 00:27:38,305
He hated dragons, after what he had seen.

512
00:27:38,835 --> 00:27:41,444
The realm called him the Broken King.

513
00:27:41,845 --> 00:27:46,375
And they called him by another
name too: Aegon the Dragonbane.

514
00:27:47,125 --> 00:27:50,575
Because during his reign,
the last dragons died.

515
00:27:51,284 --> 00:27:54,975
The last of them was a small,
sickly green female,

516
00:27:55,205 --> 00:27:59,015
who died in the hundred and fifty-third
year after the Conquest.

517
00:28:00,005 --> 00:28:04,155
And with her, the age of dragons
in Westeros seemed to end.

518
00:28:05,165 --> 00:28:06,775
Aegon tried to bring them back.

519
00:28:06,625 --> 00:28:10,565
He sent for mages from
the east, nine of them,

520
00:28:10,514 --> 00:28:12,125
to hatch the remaining eggs.

521
00:28:12,855 --> 00:28:14,225
All nine failed.

522
00:28:14,635 --> 00:28:19,485
No dragon would be born in the world
for nearly a hundred and fifty years.

523
00:28:20,615 --> 00:28:23,805
Aegon's son Daeron was the
opposite of his father.

524
00:28:24,315 --> 00:28:27,184
Bold, bright and hungry for glory.

525
00:28:28,235 --> 00:28:34,085
At fourteen, King Daeron the First set
out to finish the one thing Aegon

526
00:28:33,935 --> 00:28:35,684
the Conqueror never could.

527
00:28:35,884 --> 00:28:37,954
He conquered Dorne.

528
00:28:37,804 --> 00:28:39,404
Without a single dragon.

529
00:28:39,914 --> 00:28:41,624
He marched through the mountain passes,

530
00:28:41,814 --> 00:28:45,544
took Sunspear, and wrote a famous
account of his own victory.

531
00:28:46,054 --> 00:28:47,844
The Conquest of Dorne.

532
00:28:48,244 --> 00:28:50,074
But Dorne had not truly bent.

533
00:28:50,564 --> 00:28:53,654
It rose again behind him,
and within a few years,

534
00:28:53,504 --> 00:28:57,434
the young king was dead, struck
down under a banner of peace,

535
00:28:57,644 --> 00:28:59,774
at just eighteen years old.

536
00:29:00,204 --> 00:29:03,574
The histories say tens of thousands
died to win Dorne,

537
00:29:03,424 --> 00:29:05,634
and keep it for a single summer.

538
00:29:06,244 --> 00:29:10,334
His brother Baelor took the throne,
and the realm had never seen a king

539
00:29:10,184 --> 00:29:10,934
like him.

540
00:29:11,844 --> 00:29:14,314
Baelor the Blessed was a
septon as well as a king.

541
00:29:14,744 --> 00:29:17,614
He walked barefoot all the
way to Dorne to make peace.

542
00:29:18,384 --> 00:29:20,494
Along the way, he learned that his cousin,

543
00:29:20,804 --> 00:29:25,634
Prince Aemon the Dragonknight, was being
held in a cage above a pit of vipers.

544
00:29:26,584 --> 00:29:29,074
Baelor walked straight into
the pit to free him.

545
00:29:29,474 --> 00:29:33,294
The singers say the vipers
bowed their heads to him.

546
00:29:33,144 --> 00:29:36,234
The histories say he was
bitten many times,

547
00:29:36,604 --> 00:29:38,874
and Aemon had to carry
him out on his back.

548
00:29:39,864 --> 00:29:40,674
Baelor survived.

549
00:29:41,324 --> 00:29:43,614
And he came home stranger than ever.

550
00:29:44,344 --> 00:29:48,134
He shut his three sisters away
in a tower of the Red Keep,

551
00:29:47,984 --> 00:29:50,414
so they would not tempt
the men of the court.

552
00:29:51,424 --> 00:29:53,494
It was called the Maidenvault.

553
00:29:54,424 --> 00:29:58,814
He built the Great Sept of Baelor,
with its seven crystal towers.

554
00:29:59,384 --> 00:30:03,194
In the show, Cersei Lannister
blows it up with wildfire.

555
00:30:03,604 --> 00:30:05,674
In the books, it still stands.

556
00:30:06,784 --> 00:30:10,174
Baelor died after a long
fast, still praying.

557
00:30:11,164 --> 00:30:13,694
Then came the worst king of all.

558
00:30:14,564 --> 00:30:16,694
His name was Aegon the Fourth.

559
00:30:17,164 --> 00:30:20,294
And the histories call
him Aegon the Unworthy.

560
00:30:21,164 --> 00:30:23,914
He was greedy, lazy, and vain.

561
00:30:24,114 --> 00:30:28,024
He took mistress after mistress, and
fathered bastards across the realm.

562
00:30:28,474 --> 00:30:31,304
He tried to build wooden
dragons to invade Dorne,

563
00:30:31,454 --> 00:30:32,244
and they burned.

564
00:30:32,774 --> 00:30:35,244
But his worst act came on his deathbed.

565
00:30:35,644 --> 00:30:37,834
He legitimized all of his bastards.

566
00:30:38,234 --> 00:30:40,004
Every one of them, at once.

567
00:30:40,554 --> 00:30:43,884
And years earlier, he had done
something even more dangerous.

568
00:30:44,374 --> 00:30:48,544
He had given the sword Blackfyre,
the sword of Aegon the Conqueror,

569
00:30:48,794 --> 00:30:52,124
not to his heir, but to his
favourite bastard son,

570
00:30:52,394 --> 00:30:54,044
a young man named Daemon.

571
00:30:54,554 --> 00:30:59,404
In one stroke of a quill, he planted the
seed of a war that would last sixty

572
00:30:59,254 --> 00:31:00,004
years.

573
00:31:02,724 --> 00:31:05,594
The next king, Daeron the
Second, was a scholar.

574
00:31:06,484 --> 00:31:08,094
Gentle, wise, and bookish.

575
00:31:08,284 --> 00:31:10,404
He was called Daeron the Good.

576
00:31:10,804 --> 00:31:14,114
And he finally did what
no dragon or army could.

577
00:31:14,514 --> 00:31:16,244
He brought Dorne into the realm.

578
00:31:16,644 --> 00:31:17,874
Not with fire.

579
00:31:18,274 --> 00:31:19,064
With marriage.

580
00:31:19,464 --> 00:31:24,014
His sister wed the Prince of Dorne,
and Dorne joined the Seven Kingdoms

581
00:31:23,864 --> 00:31:25,014
in peace.

582
00:31:25,424 --> 00:31:27,414
But many lords hated it.

583
00:31:27,814 --> 00:31:29,644
They hated the Dornish at court.

584
00:31:29,914 --> 00:31:31,574
They hated the king's books.

585
00:31:32,324 --> 00:31:36,694
And they whispered that Daeron was not
really Aegon the Fourth's son at

586
00:31:36,544 --> 00:31:40,534
all, but the son of the queen
and the Dragonknight.

587
00:31:41,564 --> 00:31:46,374
And there was another man in the realm
who looked far more like a king.

588
00:31:47,104 --> 00:31:51,094
Daemon was tall, strong,
and a famous warrior.

589
00:31:51,724 --> 00:31:55,034
He carried Blackfyre, the
Conqueror's own sword.

590
00:31:56,044 --> 00:31:57,294
Knights loved him.

591
00:31:57,824 --> 00:31:58,974
And he had a claim.

592
00:31:59,584 --> 00:32:03,354
He took a new name: Daemon Blackfyre.

593
00:32:03,754 --> 00:32:06,304
And he reversed the Targaryen colours.

594
00:32:06,734 --> 00:32:09,684
Where the true king flew
a red dragon on black,

595
00:32:10,254 --> 00:32:12,824
Daemon flew a black dragon on red.

596
00:32:12,674 --> 00:32:17,514
In the hundred and ninety-sixth
year, he rose.

597
00:32:17,714 --> 00:32:21,524
The decisive battle was fought at
a place called Redgrass Field.

598
00:32:22,114 --> 00:32:24,804
On one side, the Black
Dragon and his knights.

599
00:32:25,314 --> 00:32:27,104
On the other, the king's men.

600
00:32:27,514 --> 00:32:31,084
And among the king's men was another
of Aegon the Fourth's bastards.

601
00:32:31,514 --> 00:32:36,524
A pale, strange young man, an albino,
with white hair and red eyes.

602
00:32:37,214 --> 00:32:41,444
His name was Brynden Rivers, but the
realm would call him Bloodraven.

603
00:32:42,424 --> 00:32:43,964
Bloodraven commanded the archers.

604
00:32:44,364 --> 00:32:46,734
They called themselves the Raven's Teeth.

605
00:32:47,224 --> 00:32:51,454
When Daemon Blackfyre charged,
Bloodraven's arrows found him,

606
00:32:51,304 --> 00:32:53,694
and both of his twin sons with him.

607
00:32:54,444 --> 00:32:58,334
The royal princes Baelor Breakspear
and Maekar crushed the rest.

608
00:32:59,124 --> 00:33:02,054
But the dream of the black
dragon did not die.

609
00:33:02,844 --> 00:33:06,954
Daemon's half-brother, Bittersteel,
fled across the narrow sea,

610
00:33:06,804 --> 00:33:11,554
and founded a company of exiles that would
become the most famous sellsword

611
00:33:11,404 --> 00:33:12,574
army in the world.

612
00:33:12,974 --> 00:33:14,694
The Golden Company.

613
00:33:14,544 --> 00:33:19,174
For sixty years, the Blackfyres
would rise again and again.

614
00:33:19,664 --> 00:33:21,574
Five rebellions in all.

615
00:33:21,984 --> 00:33:25,474
The last of them ended in the
two hundred and sixtieth year,

616
00:33:25,684 --> 00:33:30,834
when a young knight named Barristan Selmy
killed the last Blackfyre pretender

617
00:33:30,684 --> 00:33:32,234
in single combat.

618
00:33:33,324 --> 00:33:34,614
And Bloodraven?

619
00:33:35,044 --> 00:33:37,254
He became the Hand of the King.

620
00:33:37,744 --> 00:33:39,814
The most feared man in the realm.

621
00:33:40,214 --> 00:33:44,024
A sorcerer, people whispered,
with spies everywhere.

622
00:33:44,694 --> 00:33:46,944
There was a riddle in those years.

623
00:33:47,554 --> 00:33:50,224
How many eyes does Lord Bloodraven have?

624
00:33:51,254 --> 00:33:53,824
A thousand eyes, and one.

625
00:33:54,654 --> 00:33:59,104
A great sickness swept the realm in the
year two hundred and nine and took

626
00:33:58,954 --> 00:34:01,164
King Daeron the Good with it.

627
00:34:01,974 --> 00:34:06,384
Years later, Bloodraven was arrested,
and sent to the Wall.

628
00:34:06,584 --> 00:34:08,974
He became Lord Commander
of the Night's Watch.

629
00:34:09,424 --> 00:34:13,054
And then one day, he rode beyond
the Wall and vanished.

630
00:34:13,984 --> 00:34:17,174
If you watched our last episode,
you know where he went.

631
00:34:17,724 --> 00:34:21,374
In the books, Bran Stark finds
him deep beneath a hill,

632
00:34:21,224 --> 00:34:24,594
wound into the roots of a
weirwood, still watching,

633
00:34:24,444 --> 00:34:26,274
with his one red eye.

634
00:34:28,994 --> 00:34:32,344
Now the story comes to a small
boy with a shaved head.

635
00:34:32,194 --> 00:34:34,754
He was called Egg.

636
00:34:35,604 --> 00:34:40,574
A fourth son of a fourth son, so far
from the throne that nobody thought

637
00:34:40,424 --> 00:34:41,894
of him as a prince at all.

638
00:34:42,404 --> 00:34:46,214
As a boy, he shaved his head
to hide his Targaryen hair,

639
00:34:46,064 --> 00:34:51,834
and served as squire to a huge, kind,
poor hedge knight named Ser Duncan

640
00:34:51,684 --> 00:34:52,414
the Tall.

641
00:34:53,204 --> 00:34:58,034
Their adventures are told in the books
in three short tales of Dunk and

642
00:34:57,884 --> 00:34:58,394
Egg.

643
00:34:58,784 --> 00:35:04,234
And they are now a television series
too: A Knight of the Seven Kingdoms.

644
00:35:04,924 --> 00:35:08,214
But nobody could have guessed
where Egg would end up.

645
00:35:08,614 --> 00:35:10,804
In the two hundred and thirty-third year,

646
00:35:10,654 --> 00:35:12,884
the realm needed a new king again.

647
00:35:13,434 --> 00:35:15,384
Another Great Council was called.

648
00:35:15,914 --> 00:35:19,244
The crown was first offered
to Egg's older brother,

649
00:35:19,634 --> 00:35:19,964
Aemon.

650
00:35:20,714 --> 00:35:23,524
But Aemon had already chosen
a different life.

651
00:35:23,914 --> 00:35:27,614
He had forged a maester's
chain, and taken vows.

652
00:35:28,144 --> 00:35:29,514
He refused.

653
00:35:31,404 --> 00:35:33,434
So the lords turned to Egg.

654
00:35:34,284 --> 00:35:36,594
He became King Aegon the Fifth.

655
00:35:37,204 --> 00:35:40,394
The realm called him Aegon the Unlikely.

656
00:35:40,924 --> 00:35:45,554
And Aemon, so that no one could ever
use him against his brother,

657
00:35:46,024 --> 00:35:47,214
went to the Wall.

658
00:35:47,924 --> 00:35:51,914
He would serve the Night's Watch as
its maester for the rest of his long

659
00:35:51,764 --> 00:35:52,294
life.

660
00:35:52,964 --> 00:35:58,734
In the first book, he is the blind old
man at Castle Black who teaches Jon

661
00:35:58,584 --> 00:35:59,174
Snow.

662
00:35:59,984 --> 00:36:03,454
Very few at the Wall even
know he is a Targaryen.

663
00:36:03,654 --> 00:36:06,844
Egg had spent his boyhood on the
roads with a hedge knight.

664
00:36:07,244 --> 00:36:11,774
He had slept in ditches and inns, and
he had seen how the smallfolk lived.

665
00:36:12,324 --> 00:36:14,414
As king, he tried to help them.

666
00:36:14,814 --> 00:36:17,024
The great lords fought him at every turn.

667
00:36:17,714 --> 00:36:21,164
Ser Duncan the Tall became the Lord
Commander of his Kingsguard.

668
00:36:21,954 --> 00:36:23,944
And Egg dreamed of one more thing.

669
00:36:24,414 --> 00:36:25,784
He dreamed of dragons.

670
00:36:26,614 --> 00:36:28,844
In the two hundred and fifty-ninth year,

671
00:36:28,694 --> 00:36:31,204
the royal family gathered at Summerhall,

672
00:36:31,334 --> 00:36:33,504
a summer palace in the Dornish Marches,

673
00:36:33,674 --> 00:36:37,404
to celebrate the birth of the
king's first great-grandchild.

674
00:36:38,194 --> 00:36:39,624
Something happened there.

675
00:36:40,134 --> 00:36:41,624
Something involving fire.

676
00:36:42,094 --> 00:36:44,584
The histories hold one surviving letter,

677
00:36:44,434 --> 00:36:47,284
written by the castle's
maester before he died.

678
00:36:47,734 --> 00:36:49,764
It was ruined by a spill of ink.

679
00:36:50,274 --> 00:36:52,044
Only fragments can be read.

680
00:36:52,814 --> 00:36:55,844
The blood of the dragon, gathered in one.

681
00:36:56,814 --> 00:36:59,604
Seven eggs, to honour the seven gods.

682
00:37:00,814 --> 00:37:01,684
Pyromancers.

683
00:37:02,254 --> 00:37:03,124
Wildfire.

684
00:37:03,914 --> 00:37:06,304
The flames grew out of control.

685
00:37:06,654 --> 00:37:08,954
The fire destroyed Summerhall.

686
00:37:09,424 --> 00:37:11,614
It killed King Aegon the Fifth.

687
00:37:12,144 --> 00:37:14,574
It killed his son, Prince Duncan.

688
00:37:15,104 --> 00:37:19,874
And it killed Ser Duncan the Tall,
who died trying to save his friend.

689
00:37:20,684 --> 00:37:23,694
In the books, nobody ever says
exactly what happened.

690
00:37:24,094 --> 00:37:26,404
But the hints all point the same way.

691
00:37:26,954 --> 00:37:28,444
Egg tried to hatch dragons.

692
00:37:28,894 --> 00:37:31,884
And on that same day, in the middle
of the grief and the smoke,

693
00:37:32,334 --> 00:37:34,224
a baby was born at Summerhall.

694
00:37:34,634 --> 00:37:36,244
His name was Rhaegar.

695
00:37:37,114 --> 00:37:41,784
All his life, the histories say, Rhaegar
was drawn back to those ruins.

696
00:37:42,184 --> 00:37:45,994
He would go there alone, to
brood, and to play his harp.

697
00:37:46,724 --> 00:37:48,134
There is one more thread.

698
00:37:48,334 --> 00:37:52,624
Prince Duncan, Egg's son, gave up his
claim to the throne to marry a girl

699
00:37:52,474 --> 00:37:55,744
he loved, a girl named Jenny of Oldstones.

700
00:37:56,614 --> 00:38:00,864
Jenny had a strange friend: a tiny
woods witch from the riverlands.

701
00:38:01,514 --> 00:38:04,364
If you watched our last episode,
you may have met her.

702
00:38:04,914 --> 00:38:07,704
Many readers believe she is
the ghost of High Heart,

703
00:38:08,014 --> 00:38:12,584
the tiny old woman who weeps whenever she
hears the song of Jenny of Oldstones.

704
00:38:13,074 --> 00:38:17,824
And it was a woods witch who told the
family a prophecy: that the prince

705
00:38:17,674 --> 00:38:21,384
that was promised would be born of
the line of Aerys and Rhaella.

706
00:38:22,434 --> 00:38:26,344
So the next king married his son
Aerys to his daughter Rhaella.

707
00:38:27,194 --> 00:38:28,104
Brother and sister.

708
00:38:28,694 --> 00:38:32,344
They would be the last king and
queen of House Targaryen.

709
00:38:35,064 --> 00:38:38,074
Aerys the Second came to
the throne at eighteen,

710
00:38:38,184 --> 00:38:42,504
and at first, he seemed charming
and full of promise.

711
00:38:42,354 --> 00:38:46,264
He named his boyhood friend,
Tywin Lannister,

712
00:38:46,114 --> 00:38:47,404
as his Hand.

713
00:38:47,804 --> 00:38:50,294
And for twenty years, Tywin ran the realm,

714
00:38:50,144 --> 00:38:53,314
coldly, brilliantly, and well.

715
00:38:53,964 --> 00:38:55,534
But Aerys grew jealous.

716
00:38:56,484 --> 00:38:59,394
Jealous of Tywin's power, of his praise,

717
00:38:59,744 --> 00:39:03,074
of the way the realm credited
Tywin for every success.

718
00:39:03,824 --> 00:39:05,394
He began to mock him.

719
00:39:05,794 --> 00:39:06,984
To insult him.

720
00:39:07,384 --> 00:39:09,014
And then came Duskendale.

721
00:39:09,524 --> 00:39:13,074
A minor lord of a port town
refused to pay his taxes.

722
00:39:14,344 --> 00:39:17,874
Aerys went to Duskendale
in person, to settle it.

723
00:39:18,274 --> 00:39:22,864
The lord seized him, and held the king
of the Seven Kingdoms prisoner for

724
00:39:22,714 --> 00:39:23,564
half a year.

725
00:39:24,694 --> 00:39:29,164
Ser Barristan Selmy finally slipped
into the town alone and brought him

726
00:39:29,014 --> 00:39:29,504
out.

727
00:39:30,114 --> 00:39:33,504
But the man who came out was
not the man who went in.

728
00:39:34,194 --> 00:39:36,624
Afterwards, Aerys would
not leave the Red Keep.

729
00:39:37,174 --> 00:39:38,604
He trusted no one.

730
00:39:38,804 --> 00:39:40,814
He would not let a blade come near him,

731
00:39:40,844 --> 00:39:43,174
so he stopped cutting his
hair and his nails.

732
00:39:43,574 --> 00:39:45,744
They grew long, tangled and yellow.

733
00:39:46,474 --> 00:39:47,964
And he found a new obsession.

734
00:39:48,574 --> 00:39:49,104
Fire.

735
00:39:49,694 --> 00:39:51,964
He surrounded himself with pyromancers,

736
00:39:52,334 --> 00:39:56,744
the alchemists of the wildfire guild,
and the whole court lived in terror

737
00:39:56,594 --> 00:39:57,524
of the flames.

738
00:39:59,094 --> 00:40:01,384
In the two hundred and eighty-first year,

739
00:40:01,534 --> 00:40:03,744
a great tourney was held at Harrenhal.

740
00:40:04,154 --> 00:40:05,994
Prince Rhaegar won it.

741
00:40:06,044 --> 00:40:10,914
And as the champion, he was meant to crown
a lady as queen of love and beauty.

742
00:40:11,964 --> 00:40:13,874
Everyone expected him to crown his wife,

743
00:40:14,304 --> 00:40:15,654
Elia Martell of Dorne.

744
00:40:16,224 --> 00:40:20,694
Instead, he rode past her, and laid
a crown of blue winter roses in the

745
00:40:20,544 --> 00:40:21,794
lap of Lyanna Stark.

746
00:40:22,444 --> 00:40:26,794
In the first book, Ned Stark remembers
that moment as the moment all the

747
00:40:26,644 --> 00:40:27,574
smiles died.

748
00:40:28,244 --> 00:40:31,334
A year later, Rhaegar and Lyanna
disappeared together.

749
00:40:32,024 --> 00:40:36,174
Lyanna's brother Brandon rode to King's
Landing and demanded that Rhaegar

750
00:40:36,024 --> 00:40:37,374
come out and face him.

751
00:40:37,924 --> 00:40:40,774
Neither Brandon nor his father,
Lord Rickard Stark,

752
00:40:40,904 --> 00:40:42,854
ever left the Red Keep alive.

753
00:40:43,584 --> 00:40:47,594
Then Aerys demanded Eddard Stark
and Robert Baratheon too.

754
00:40:48,584 --> 00:40:51,774
Their foster father, Jon Arryn, refused.

755
00:40:52,444 --> 00:40:53,754
And the realm rose.

756
00:40:55,004 --> 00:40:59,514
At the Trident, Robert Baratheon
met Rhaegar in the river.

757
00:41:00,264 --> 00:41:03,134
Robert's great warhammer broke
Rhaegar's breastplate,

758
00:41:03,384 --> 00:41:05,074
and Rhaegar fell in the river.

759
00:41:05,944 --> 00:41:10,714
Its rubies scattered into the water, and
men dove for them for years afterward.

760
00:41:11,324 --> 00:41:13,814
The place is still called the Ruby Ford.

761
00:41:15,164 --> 00:41:19,294
In King's Landing, Tywin Lannister
arrived with an army,

762
00:41:19,144 --> 00:41:21,594
claiming to come to the king's aid.

763
00:41:22,884 --> 00:41:24,194
Aerys opened the gates.

764
00:41:24,704 --> 00:41:27,314
And the Lannister army
poured into the city.

765
00:41:27,514 --> 00:41:32,184
And in the throne room, a young knight
of the Kingsguard named Jaime Lannister

766
00:41:32,034 --> 00:41:34,924
heard the king chanting the same words,

767
00:41:34,774 --> 00:41:36,284
over and over.

768
00:41:36,754 --> 00:41:37,684
Burn them all.

769
00:41:38,934 --> 00:41:42,604
Aerys had hidden caches of wildfire
beneath the entire city.

770
00:41:43,154 --> 00:41:45,844
Jaime stopped him, at the
foot of the Iron Throne.

771
00:41:47,034 --> 00:41:48,964
The Mad King's reign was over.

772
00:41:49,364 --> 00:41:52,654
For the rest of his life, the realm
would call him Kingslayer.

773
00:41:53,384 --> 00:41:56,974
In the books, he tells the
true story only once,

774
00:41:56,824 --> 00:42:00,314
to Brienne of Tarth, in
a bath at Harrenhal.

775
00:42:01,324 --> 00:42:04,154
Rhaegar's small children
were lost in the sack.

776
00:42:04,644 --> 00:42:07,974
And far to the south, in a tower
in the mountains of Dorne,

777
00:42:08,504 --> 00:42:12,414
Lyanna Stark lay dying, and made
her brother promise something.

778
00:42:13,104 --> 00:42:14,054
Promise me, Ned.

779
00:42:14,504 --> 00:42:17,514
The books never tell us what he promised.

780
00:42:20,231 --> 00:42:22,661
But the Targaryens were
not quite finished.

781
00:42:23,231 --> 00:42:27,321
Before the city fell, Queen Rhaella
had fled to Dragonstone,

782
00:42:27,171 --> 00:42:29,301
with her younger son Viserys.

783
00:42:29,701 --> 00:42:30,991
She was heavily pregnant.

784
00:42:31,521 --> 00:42:35,771
And as Robert's fleet gathered,
a great storm struck the island,

785
00:42:35,621 --> 00:42:38,751
and wrecked the Targaryen ships at anchor.

786
00:42:39,601 --> 00:42:43,111
In the middle of that storm, Rhaella
gave birth to a daughter,

787
00:42:42,961 --> 00:42:44,431
and passed away.

788
00:42:44,981 --> 00:42:46,831
The girl was named Daenerys.

789
00:42:47,561 --> 00:42:49,111
Daenerys Stormborn.

790
00:42:49,881 --> 00:42:54,111
A loyal knight smuggled the two children
across the sea to Braavos.

791
00:42:54,901 --> 00:42:59,310
Years later, Daenerys would remember only
one happy place from her childhood:

792
00:42:59,160 --> 00:43:04,451
a big house with a red door, and
a lemon tree outside her window.

793
00:43:05,501 --> 00:43:09,111
Then the knight died,
and the money ran out.

794
00:43:10,061 --> 00:43:12,711
Viserys took his sister from city to city,

795
00:43:12,841 --> 00:43:14,971
selling their mother's crown to eat.

796
00:43:14,821 --> 00:43:19,641
Behind his back, people called
him the beggar king.

797
00:43:19,841 --> 00:43:21,851
And then Viserys sold Daenerys too.

798
00:43:22,251 --> 00:43:24,921
He married her to a Dothraki
warlord, Khal Drogo,

799
00:43:24,971 --> 00:43:27,241
in exchange for an army that never came.

800
00:43:27,671 --> 00:43:30,041
Among her wedding gifts
were three dragon eggs,

801
00:43:30,091 --> 00:43:31,681
turned to stone by the centuries.

802
00:43:32,291 --> 00:43:34,161
Viserys did get his crown in the end.

803
00:43:34,561 --> 00:43:37,271
A crown of molten gold,
poured by Khal Drogo,

804
00:43:37,121 --> 00:43:39,371
when he grew tired of Viserys's threats.

805
00:43:39,741 --> 00:43:41,561
He was no dragon, Daenerys thought.

806
00:43:42,091 --> 00:43:43,561
Fire cannot kill a dragon.

807
00:43:44,611 --> 00:43:47,781
When Drogo died, Daenerys
built him a funeral pyre,

808
00:43:47,891 --> 00:43:51,001
set her three stone eggs on it,
and walked into the flames.

809
00:43:51,451 --> 00:43:53,401
In the morning, she rose from the ashes,

810
00:43:53,671 --> 00:43:54,321
unburnt.

811
00:43:54,731 --> 00:43:57,201
And three newborn dragons
were clinging to her.

812
00:43:57,411 --> 00:44:00,611
One black, one green, one cream and gold.

813
00:44:01,221 --> 00:44:01,711
Drogon.

814
00:44:02,261 --> 00:44:02,631
Rhaegal.

815
00:44:03,181 --> 00:44:03,851
Viserion.

816
00:44:04,601 --> 00:44:08,311
The first dragons to be born in the world
for nearly a century and a half.

817
00:44:08,921 --> 00:44:12,071
In the books that followed, Daenerys
crossed the red waste,

818
00:44:12,301 --> 00:44:14,871
freed the slaves of Astapor,
Yunkai and Meereen,

819
00:44:15,041 --> 00:44:17,811
and ruled Meereen as its queen, trying,

820
00:44:17,661 --> 00:44:20,631
and often failing, to make
a broken city work.

821
00:44:20,821 --> 00:44:25,821
At the end of the fifth book, Drogon
carries her out of a fighting pit and

822
00:44:25,671 --> 00:44:27,601
far into the Dothraki Sea.

823
00:44:28,031 --> 00:44:30,001
That is where her story stops.

824
00:44:30,551 --> 00:44:31,261
For now.

825
00:44:32,311 --> 00:44:35,181
But she is not the only Targaryen
left in the books.

826
00:44:35,911 --> 00:44:40,321
Old Maester Aemon, Egg's brother,
the last Targaryen at the Wall,

827
00:44:40,911 --> 00:44:45,121
dies at sea on his way to Oldtown,
murmuring about dragons,

828
00:44:44,971 --> 00:44:46,561
and about her.

829
00:44:47,391 --> 00:44:50,981
In his last moments, he calls
for his little brother.

830
00:44:51,751 --> 00:44:52,241
Egg.

831
00:44:53,091 --> 00:44:55,441
I dreamed that I was old.

832
00:44:55,641 --> 00:44:59,111
In the fifth book, a young man
called Griff appears in Essos,

833
00:44:58,961 --> 00:45:03,311
claiming to be Rhaegar's son, Aegon,
saved from the sack as a baby.

834
00:45:03,711 --> 00:45:06,981
And the army marching behind
him is the Golden Company.

835
00:45:07,431 --> 00:45:11,241
The sellswords founded by Bittersteel,
the Blackfyre exile.

836
00:45:11,891 --> 00:45:15,521
Many readers suspect he is
not who he claims to be.

837
00:45:15,691 --> 00:45:19,171
That he may be a Blackfyre,
at last coming home.

838
00:45:19,021 --> 00:45:21,601
The books have not said.

839
00:45:22,351 --> 00:45:24,621
And at the Wall, there is Jon Snow.

840
00:45:25,031 --> 00:45:27,701
A bastard of Winterfell,
the son of Ned Stark.

841
00:45:28,101 --> 00:45:29,571
Or so everyone believes.

842
00:45:30,261 --> 00:45:34,971
In the show, it is confirmed: Jon
is the son of Rhaegar and Lyanna,

843
00:45:35,201 --> 00:45:37,571
and his true name is Aegon Targaryen.

844
00:45:37,971 --> 00:45:42,161
In the books, it is one of the most
famous theories ever written about a

845
00:45:42,011 --> 00:45:43,681
story that has not finished yet.

846
00:45:43,531 --> 00:45:46,071
The hints are all there.

847
00:45:46,471 --> 00:45:47,321
Promise me, Ned.

848
00:45:48,571 --> 00:45:50,621
The show gave the dynasty an ending.

849
00:45:51,091 --> 00:45:54,121
Daenerys burned King's Landing,
Jon killed her,

850
00:45:54,211 --> 00:45:56,261
and Drogon melted the Iron Throne.

851
00:45:56,661 --> 00:45:59,551
In the books, that ending
has not been written.

852
00:45:59,951 --> 00:46:02,581
The Winds of Winter is still unpublished.

853
00:46:02,971 --> 00:46:06,011
And so is the second half
of Fire and Blood.

854
00:46:06,861 --> 00:46:10,431
So the history of House
Targaryen is still open.

855
00:46:10,801 --> 00:46:15,061
It began, three hundred years ago,
with a girl who dreamed of fire.

856
00:46:15,631 --> 00:46:18,321
It may end with a girl who walked into it.

857
00:46:19,719 --> 00:46:21,849
So who was the greatest Targaryen?

858
00:46:22,249 --> 00:46:24,839
Aegon the Conqueror, who built
the realm with fire?

859
00:46:25,789 --> 00:46:27,799
Jaehaerys, who made it work?

860
00:46:28,449 --> 00:46:31,099
Egg, the unlikely king who
loved the smallfolk?

861
00:46:31,549 --> 00:46:34,079
Or Daenerys, whose story is not over?

862
00:46:34,549 --> 00:46:35,699
Tell us in the comments.

863
00:46:36,109 --> 00:46:37,999
And if you want more of the
books brought to life,

864
00:46:38,229 --> 00:46:41,059
like this video, and subscribe
to the Mythic Archives.

865
00:46:41,609 --> 00:46:44,629
Next, we go north of the
Wall, to the Others.

866
00:46:44,479 --> 00:46:47,689
And what the books really say about them.
